NAME
    results - the store's answers

SYNOPSIS
    results [--last N]
    results --slowest N [--tier T] [--since D]
    results --flaky [--since D] | --misses [--since D] | --quarantine
    results --selected TRIAL
    results unit UNIT | test NAME
    results export [--since D]

DESCRIPTION
    A command of the emusen.testing module; it only reads. The store is
    ~/.local/share/EmuSen/testing/studio.db (EMUSEN_TESTING_DB for
    another). D is a span such as 14d, 12h or 30m.

        (none)       the last trials: number, start, verdict, tier, tree,
                     branch, time and the source a backfilled one came from
        --slowest    units by median wall time, with runs and the maximum
        --flaky      tests recorded flaky, with their runners, and tests
                     with two outcomes under one key
        --misses     impact's misses as the nightly records them
        --quarantine the quarantine in force
        --selected   why each unit was in a trial: reason, file, key, and
                     the trial a reused unit came from
        unit, test   history, the newest first
        export       every trial since D as one JSON object a line

    Units read back from land.sh's old logs are named as land.sh ran them:
    a crate folder, and 'dotnet:EmuSen.WiseMan' for a dotnet step without
    a TRX file. See EmuSen_Testing.md §3.5.

EXAMPLES
    results --slowest 15 --tier land
    results --flaky --since 14d
    results unit "cargo:EmuSen/Cores/Sony/Sapphire - PlayStation 2"
    results test Every_audited_window_state
    results export --since 30d > trials.jsonl
